      "content": "That \"adventurer\" comparison is a bit much, but I get the sentiment. \n\nTo be more specific about the \"trickery\" part—we've noticed these discrepancies often occur around certain types of assets, like small, hard-to-trace petty cash accounts or complex, multi-currency digital wallets. It's almost like someone is skimming just enough to stay under the radar, but doing it with enough frequency to create a mess. \n\nIn your professional opinion, when these discrepancies appear to be \"playing games\" with the numbers, what specific forensic techniques are used to pin down whether it's a software error or a person intentionally manipulating the system to create these little \"ghost\" entries?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
